>> title: Menma
>> category: Toppings & Pickles
>> tags: japanese, bamboo, ramen, topping, side
>> counters: Ramen Shop, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: menma, メンマ, 麺麻, seasoned bamboo shoots, fermented bamboo shoots, shinachiku, bamboo shoot topping, ramen bamboo
>> pairs-with: shoyu-ramen, dashi
>> servings: 8
>> time: 9 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the simmer is taken to nearly dry, and a pan that goes past it catches the sugar and turns the whole batch bitter
>> step.1: Salted and fermented, sold in a bag in the chiller — not the tinned bamboo in water.
>> step.2: soak 8 hr, then boil 20 min
>> step.3: fry in sesame oil 3 min
>> step.4: simmer down until dry, 15 min

Salted and fermented, sold in a bag in the chiller — not the tinned bamboo in water, which stays crunchy and tastes of nothing.

Soak @salted bamboo shoots{8%oz}(225 g; shinachiku) in @water{4%cups}(950 mL) ~soak{8%hr}, changing the water twice, then boil them in fresh water ~boil{20%min} and taste a piece. It should read as seasoned, not salty; if it is still sharp, boil it again in clean water for ten minutes.

Fry @&(~1)drained bamboo{}, sliced into 2-inch batons, in @toasted sesame oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) over high heat ~fry{3%min}, until the edges catch and it squeaks against the pan.

Simmer @&(~1)bamboo{} in @dashi{1%cup}(240 mL) with @soy sauce{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @mirin{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @granulated sugar{2%tsp}(8 g) and @dried chilli{1}(sliced) ~simmer{15%min}, until the pan is nearly dry and the batons are glossy. It keeps a week, and it is better on the second day.
